From 35e28ad55e4ceed63ccddd3f2d387628ef380417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:42:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): resolve authored Bedrock server UI scenes

Evaluate loaded JSON UI templates, scoped variables, collection bindings
and bounded native string expressions against each server form. Preserve
original form IDs and button indices when projecting Java dialogs or
sending a negotiated native rendering scene to a client integration.
Keep pack texture bytes and nine-slice metadata in the converted pack,
and include the versioned built-in UI identity in conversion fingerprints.

Target Bedrock 1.26.51.1 and protocol 2193. Original native evaluator,
variable precedence and missing-template factory controls inform the
implementation: omit an unavailable child template while retaining its
siblings. Optional licensed UI archives are supplied at build time;
missing assets or unsupported scenes retain the ordinary form flow.
Native GPU, font, full binding-controller and animation parity remain
separate verification work. No local game installation is required.

Actual protocol2193 CubeCraft forms use typed elements rather than the
legacy buttons array. Normalize decoded forms through MCStructs and keep
full collection positions separate from button response ordinals. Four
original native decoder/click controls establish legacy precedence and
header/label/divider positions, without inferring native GPU behavior.

Preserve authored HTTPS image URLs and file-system bindings in the scene.
The client renderer loads their bytes asynchronously; packet and resource
workers do not perform network image downloads.

Normalize accepted JPEG and TGA UI textures to PNG using the existing
content decoders, retain native per-layer image priority and metadata,
and bound dimensions before decoding. Actual accepted server assets use
JPEG for Loot and gifting images; omitting them forced whole-form fallback.
Version the UI conversion identity so prior PNG-only caches are rebuilt.

Resolve explicit source extensions and their metadata to the normalized
PNG identity. Validate PNG dimensions before client decoding and permit
upper-layer replacements at the texture limit without adding entries.

Resolve native custom forms through a separately negotiated capability.
Share the same bounded core program for initial and local input-state
resolution, retaining all original response positions and null prose
slots. Expose toggle, input, scalar and step sliders, and nested dropdown
state with actual native bindings and resource language captions.

Keep the existing Java dialog available for unsupported controls, missing
assets and client rendering errors. Reuse the tracked form and dialog
construction for explicit fallback without discarding response identity.
The pinned form library lacks multiselect support, so that type retains
the ordinary flow. Native slider geometry and live custom responses remain
separate verification work.

Retain native slider and thumb named state subtrees while their inactive
computed visibility remains false. Original native visibility setters
activate authored hidden hover and locked branches, so pruning their
descendants loses required captions, textures and bindings. Preserve
each descendant's own bound visibility separately for selected-state
activation without overriding unrelated hidden controls or input indices.

Pinned native slider fixtures pass 184 controls for geometry, pointer
coordinates, state selection, progress clipping and value publication.
These CPU fixtures do not establish native GPU or coupled input dispatch.

Share one JsonUiProgram for form and container definitions, scoped bindings,
named collections, factories, textures and language data. FormBindings
retains original response ordinals and custom input state; ContainerUi
binds native chest collections to actual Java menu slot identities.
Distinguish singleton factories from repeating grid factories and retain
outer scope when selecting another collection explicitly.

Deliver bounded native_container programs only after the actual Java
OPEN_SCREEN and only under its negotiated capability. Keep connection-local
presentation sequencing independent of inventory revisions and requests.
Java content, cursor, close and click packets remain authoritative. Retain
raw available title conditions separately from the displayed title without
inferring names from held items. Unsupported families and programs keep
the original screen; frontend rendering failures retain its ordinary menu.

Targeted production codec/packet tests verify both chest sizes, actual
packet order, repeated menu IDs, capability fallback and payload bounds.
Private target 1.26.51.1 definitions and the accepted server pack resolve
and round-trip every 3-row and 6-row slot with no missing templates.
Native actor title/size, transient inventory renderers, coupled input and
native pixels remain verification boundaries, not parity claims.

Retain typed count-label provenance in container scenes from authored text
and binding sources, including variable aliases and selected cursor counts.
Expose the original merged control to the domain decorator without changing
form actions. An unrelated later text binding clears the count annotation.
The frontend can draw real Java stack counts once at that authored geometry
while retaining unrelated numeric labels; no control-name heuristic is used.

Preserve authored members when a higher resource-pack layer partially
overrides the same namespace and control name. Keep an existing explicit
parent until an upper declaration supplies another parent, and retain
top-level replacement for controls and binding arrays.

Versioned target UI and accepted server inputs contain partial count,
chest-title, keyboard-image and text-entry-label declarations without a
type. Whole-definition replacement erased their lower type and bindings.
This layering behavior is inferred from those target inputs; original
native definition-store merge execution remains separate verification.
Four regression cases and actual three/six-row scene probes retain the
63/90 native count labels, title labels and real collection addresses.

Keep known inactive action/custom controller collections empty when both
controllers occur in the authored screen. Empty counterpart length bindings
prevent factories from manufacturing rows of the wrong form type. Preserve
unknown-collection rejection, real input state and original response indices.

Select actor-owned chest titles from retained typed NAME and nonempty
FILTERED_NAME metadata at container open. The pinned native actor getter
and metadata reader execute twelve controls for precedence, type rejection,
removal admission and empty-name dispatch. Initial scene publication sets
actor title localization separately from the untouched condition string.

Share one opening title result between Java OPEN_SCREEN and the exported
native program. Retain raw title and localization globals on program import
so authored conditions never use an already translated Java caption.
Keep physical Java custom-name translation and default captions unchanged.
Empty actor class titles, size admission, metadata updates after opening,
and actual Social actor metadata delivery remain verification boundaries.

Resolve manual grid collection ordinals before descendant bindings. The
pinned native GridItem writer uses columns * row + column, and its lookup
precedes explicit CollectionItem indices while retaining unrelated scopes.
Ignored controls do not consume addresses; malformed, overflowing and
unavailable actual collection entries keep the ordinary fallback.

Sixteen original index controls and six fresh native layout controls bind
these rules for Bedrock 1.26.51.1/protocol2193. Complex Java regressions
cover sparse and hidden controls, nested collections, conflicting indices,
round trips and invalid positions without allocating declared capacity.
Authored actor-menu subsets still require a separate frontend admission
review; this change does not fabricate slots or actor metadata delivery.

Negotiate authored manual container action scope separately from legacy
presentation bytes. Preserve referenced slot identities, bounded typed
custom-name/lore hover text and connection-local activation ownership.
The genuine server-authoritative request adapter remains in deferred
inventory work; portable UI has no request-engine compile dependency.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 original item text and count-one planner controls justify
the scoped semantics. Controlled real-item CPU projection is separate
from actual actor-backed Social delivery, native pixels and server action
acceptance. Unknown item text retains ordinary fallback.

Resolve metadata-selected acquired TTF families to isolated Java font resources with default glyph fallback. Normalize EM size and baseline against pinned native hhea metrics; unsupported formats keep existing font fallback. Carry family IDs through scene transport without requiring a local game installation.

Accept server forms that replace an inventory, closing the container through its normal pending acknowledgement path before publishing the form. Native protocol-2193 CubeCraft Friends and Parties deliver the form before container close; treating any open inventory as UserBusy made both buttons inert. Keep busy-form rejection and prevent the late inventory acknowledgement from dismissing its replacement.
